  "context_pill": "Business Income & TDS Compliance",
  "example_summary": "Delta Ltd. failed to deduct TDS on Salary and Directors' Remuneration in March 2026, leading to a 30% disallowance under Section 40(a)(ia).",
  "source_provision": "| Statutory Provision | Tax Event | Disallowance Rate |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Section 40(a)(ia) | Non-deduction of TDS on resident payments | 30% of expenditure |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Scope of Disallowance:\n> The disallowance applies to any sum payable to a resident on which tax is deductible under Chapter XVII-B. This includes salary (Section 192) and directors' remuneration (Section 194).\n\n> [!WARNING] Timing of TDS:\n> - Salary: Deductible at the time of payment.\n> - Directors' Remuneration: Deductible at the time of credit to the account of the payee or payment, whichever is earlier.\n\n- Failure to deduct TDS results in the disallowance of 30% of the relevant expenditure in the year of debit.\n- The disallowed amount is allowed as a deduction in the subsequent financial year if the tax is deducted and remitted to the Government within the prescribed timeframe.",
